.TH "XmClipboardBeginCopy" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmClipboardBeginCopy\fP \(em A clipboard function that sets up a storage area for a clipboard copy
.iX "XmClipboardBeginCopy"
.iX "clipboard functions" "XmClipboardBeginCopy"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/CutPaste\&.h>
\fBint \fBXmClipboardBeginCopy\fP\fR(
\fBDisplay *\fBdisplay\fR\fR,
\fBWindow \fBwindow\fR\fR,
\fBXmString \fBlabel\fR\fR,
\fBWidget \fBwidget\fR\fR,
\fBVoidProc \fBcallback\fR\fR,
\fBlong *\fBitemid\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmClipboardBeginCopy\fP is the Motif 1\&.1 form of
\fB\%XmClipboardStartCopy\fP: it calls \fB\%XmClipboardStartCopy\fP with
the
time stamp \fB\%CurrentTime\fP, and with \fIcallback\fP as the procedure
that
supplies data passed by name\&.  New code should use
\fB\%XmClipboardStartCopy\fP, which takes the time of the event that
started the copy\&.
.IP "\fIdisplay\fP" 10
Specifies the display\&.
.IP "\fIwindow\fP" 10
Specifies the window of the application\&.
.IP "\fIlabel\fP" 10
Specifies the label of the data item, or NULL\&.
.IP "\fIwidget\fP" 10
Specifies the widget that receives the requests for data passed by
name\&.
.IP "\fIcallback\fP" 10
Specifies the procedure called for data passed by name, or NULL\&.
.IP "\fIitemid\fP" 10
Returns the identifier of the data item\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns the status of \fB\%XmClipboardStartCopy\fP:
\fB\%XmClipboardSuccess\fP or \fB\%XmClipboardLocked\fP\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmClipboardStartCopy\fP(3), \fB\%XmClipboardCopy\fP(3) and
\fB\%XmClipboardEndCopy\fP(3)\&.
